# T7b -- The cavern ceiling, rebuilt on frequency and gated properly. T7's ceiling closed pool entries exactly as designed and achieved nothing, because entry quantity gates nothing underground. This enforces the same ceiling by holding managed cavern species at frequency 1 while the layer is over it and restoring them under it — the v5.8.1 CAVERN lever. Ceiling 12, against a control with no ceiling. A season, two replicates each. NOTE: a first attempt used a ceiling of 25, chosen from T7's numbers — but T7's counter still included the magma sea and the underworld, so it overstated the cavern layer by five to eight units. With those excluded the population never exceeded 17 and the ceiling never engaged. Twelve sits below the observed band of 16-17, so it must engage, and the layer must then fall below it to release.
run 20260918-163512 fort CTRL backup CTRL.preverify
